115:| [`/sc:issue`](#scissue---github-issue-claim-and-create) | Claim a GitHub issue (assign, accuracy check, summary, next-step prompt) or create a templated issue | `issue.md` | Yes (posts to GitHub; writes `.dev/issues/`) |
349:**When to use:** Take an existing GitHub issue on the repository `origin` points at, or file a new one. `--claim` assigns the issue to you, checks whether its text is still accurate against today's code and the pull requests merged since it was opened, writes a summary (with an effort estimate in hours) and a next-step prompt under `.dev/issues/<N>/`, posts an accuracy-check comment and a claim comment, then stops. `--create` turns a description into an issue built from one of four templates (feature or bug, simple or complex) with labels from a fixed set.
389:- It ends its summary by pointing you to `/sc:graph status` to see whether this worktree's code-graph index is ready; it never runs `/sc:graph` itself.
760:| `--report <path>` | none | Also write a summary to this path |
793:| `--summary` | Pass/fail counts only (the default) |
